# EPIC-OE-AGENTS-CONSOLIDATION-001: Current Route Usability and Classified Host Parity

**Epic ID:** `EPIC-OE-AGENTS-CONSOLIDATION-001`
**AuthorityEffect:** None
**Status:** `LIVE`

**Lifecycle scope:** Live residual audit; earlier absorption milestones are historical
**Domain Root:** [.agents](../../../../.agents/)
**Execution Discipline:** Local first; UTF-8 without BOM; classified four-host parity

## Current obstruction and bounded goal

Historical consolidation into rip-testing/rip-thanatos is not a current implementation instruction. Those routes have been retired in the present estate. Use current Woland specialization and discovery contracts; do not revive deleted aliases or silently redirect every role into another agent.

The actual parity ports are [host_root_parity.py](../../../../omega_engine_operations/use_cases/packaging/host_root_parity.py) and [sync_cross_host_skills.py](../../../../omega_engine_operations/use_cases/packaging/sync_cross_host_skills.py). They must compare intended active content while retaining explicit canon-only, host-specific, archive, quarantine and run-state classifications. A fixed persona or directory count is not a usability oracle.

## Residual sequence and acceptance

1. Produce a read-only route/dependency inventory for one agent/skill/workflow package. Resolve its actual entry point, references, license and host discovery status.
2. Verify byte-level package parity in scratch four-host roots, including referenced files and encoding. Treat extra, missing and drifted content as distinct findings.
3. Propose retirement only for a concretely unreferenced route with a recorded replacement or intentional end of discovery. Keep live references as a blocking witness.
4. Verify current canonical-to-mirror sync; do not implement a bidirectional source merge or remove exclusions wholesale.

A passing comparison supports the enumerated file custody claim only. This epic carries no deletion, deployment, authority or workflow-success receipt; old completed checkboxes are historical context and are superseded by this current residual scope.

## Obstruction review and TDD test plan

**Review basis (2026-10-10):** The old rip-testing/rip-thanatos absorption targets are historical/deleted routes, not current consolidation destinations. Current host_root_parity and sync_cross_host_skills already implement inventory comparison and controlled mirroring. Replace blanket pruning with a dry-run dependency and discovery audit; preserve host-specific, canon-only, archive and quarantine classifications.

**Bounded behavior and public port:** Call compare_root/compare_all over a temporary canonical tree and three mirrors, then compare_skill_trees/package_tree_hash and sync_skills only on scratch hosts. Input is explicit canonical/mirror paths and declared exclusions; output is classified missing/drifted/extra findings and a package receipt. Canonical .agents ownership is one-way, not a bidirectional merge.

**Dependencies and review routing:** Implement one case at a time after the stated dependency is available. Hella checks malformed input; Jeremy/Techne implements the smallest production change; Koroviev and the Soviet Inspector challenge the independent oracle; Yaroslava checks custody before Woland records the scoped result. Use the four stages intake, implementation, adversarial QA, and receipt review. Stop after at most three repair attempts and retain the blocking witness.

| Order | RED witness → minimal GREEN → refactor | Proposed test and independent oracle |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | A one-byte mirror drift and one missing file must be reported; correct only comparison/classification if needed; restore bytes and recover a clean four-host comparison. | Extend `omega_engine_operations/tests/packaging/test_host_root_parity.py::test_scratch_host_drift_and_recovery`; independent raw byte comparison on four temporary roots. |
| 2 | An archive/canon-only exclusion must not hide a new active workflow path; implement narrow explicit exclusion semantics; accept the intended exempt file while still finding active drift. | Extend `omega_engine_operations/tests/packaging/test_host_root_parity.py::test_exemption_does_not_mask_active_workflow`; hand-enumerated paths, no production exemption helper as oracle. |
| 3 | A scratch skill with an omitted reference or BOM must fail package parity; mirror the complete valid package and recover the expected independently computed digest. | Extend `omega_engine_operations/tests/packaging/test_sync_cross_host_skills.py::test_reference_custody_and_bom_controls`; full sorted path/byte manifest and UTF-8 prefix check. |
| 4 | A proposed deletion of a discoverable route with a live inbound reference must refuse dry-run planning; implement the smallest read-only dependency report first; accept a truly unreferenced retired fixture only. | Proposed `omega_engine_operations/tests/packaging/test_agent_route_retirement.py::test_live_reference_blocks_retirement`; two tiny manifests and explicit expected inbound edge. No live agent deletion in this slice. |

**Theoretical Minimum:** INVARIANT: the bounded behavior above. BREAK: the negative inputs in the ordered slices. WITNESS: actual returned value/refusal plus persisted bytes or send counts, compared with the stated independent oracle. MUTATION: Broaden SKIP_PARTS in [host_root_parity.py](../../../../omega_engine_operations/use_cases/packaging/host_root_parity.py) to hide an active workflow and require the finding test to fail. Omit a package reference from [sync_cross_host_skills.py](../../../../omega_engine_operations/use_cases/packaging/sync_cross_host_skills.py) and require its digest/path witness to fail. Route-retirement mutation awaits its proposed report implementation. Source existence was checked for this plan; mutation execution and RED recovery are still prospective. Do not count a mock-only verdict or a skipped native test as verification.

**Proposed small-batch commands:** Run each named test first with `-k <test_name>` to demonstrate RED, implement the minimum GREEN, then run the one-file regression command below before refactoring. Paths labeled proposed are not claimed to exist. Commands are not execution receipts.

~~~powershell
py -3.12 -m pytest omega_engine_operations/tests/packaging/test_host_root_parity.py -q
py -3.12 -m pytest omega_engine_operations/tests/packaging/test_sync_cross_host_skills.py -q
py -3.12 -m pytest omega_engine_operations/tests/packaging/test_agent_route_retirement.py -q
~~~

**Cross-epic sink ownership:** Governance owns canonical contracts and decision schemas; Government Councils owns roster/attribution and deliberation applications; Operations owns classified packaging/parity; Woland owns digestion orchestration while omega_intelligence owns native lifecycle decisions. Skill/rule/antibody outputs enter their owning admission queue as candidates, with source/target digest custody. A producer supplies immutable source evidence; the consumer validates its own contract and emits its own scoped receipt. No downstream plan may reuse a producer PASS as an admission decision.

**Scope and evidence ceiling:** Scratch parity verifies compared files, not workflow effectiveness or universal discovery isolation. A future retirement requires exact dependency evidence and review; do not recreate deleted rip-* routes or delete live personas to satisfy a historical count. Record any eventual SoftwareQaReceiptV1 with exact command, runtime version, exit status, tested scope, base/head and source digests, failing input, mutation diff, and recovery output outside `plans/epics/`. This planning update executes none of these proposed tests and grants no runtime or admission authority.


Cross-epic ownership and retained custody follow the [integration decision](../../decisions/adr_20261010_epic_integration_ownership.md).
